  "body": "## What changed\n\nPR #1825 added `site/tests/test_operation_reference.py`. It pins the 44 operation pictures against the `OpType` enum. Nothing ran it. The four other site tests that build the site with Zola had the same problem.\n\n- `.github/workflows/release.yml`, job `site`: a new step `Site tests`, after `Install pinned Zola` and before `Version the site is built from`. It runs `python3 -m unittest discover -s site/tests -v` with `ZOLA: /tmp/zola` (the pinned v0.23.6 that the job already installs and checks).\n  - It runs the full site suite, not only the operation reference file. This is the command that `site/README.md` already gives, and all 61 tests pass. Thus the guide navigation, image, icon and troubleshooting tests also get a run. Dropped option: one file only (`test_operation_reference.py`), which leaves the other Zola tests with no run.\n  - It runs before `version.toml` exists, on the same tree as a local run.\n  - No `continue-on-error`: a red site test fails the `site` job, and thus `pages` does not deploy.\n- `site/README.md`: one paragraph says that the release runs the same command, and how the tests find Zola.\n- No trigger, permission, runner or other job changes. `python3` is on `ubuntu-latest`.\n\n## Tests\n\nPinned by `the_site_job_runs_the_site_tests_with_its_pinned_zola` (new file `xtask/tests/release_site_tests.rs`, in the same form as `xtask/tests/post_merge_concurrency.rs`). It reads the `site` job and asserts:\n- the `Site tests` step comes after `Install pinned Zola`;\n- it runs `python3 -m unittest discover -s site/tests -v`;\n- it sets `ZOLA: /tmp/zola`;\n- it has no `continue-on-error`.\n\nWithout the workflow step, the test fails with `the site job runs the site tests (#1832)`.\n\nReadings (Linux, the pinned Zola v0.23.6, sha256 checked):\n- `ZOLA=<pinned zola> python3 -m unittest discover -s site/tests`: 61 tests, OK, 11 s.\n- With one picture line removed from `operations-2d.md` (`operation-paths.svg#Slot`): the suite fails, with `Slot needs its toolpath picture` among the failures. The file was restored.\n- Quick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`): `xtask unit tests` ok (the new test ran and passed).\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- The workflow YAML parses (`yaml.safe_load`); the site steps start `Install pinned Zola`, `Site tests`, `Version the site is built from`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No real `release.yml` run. The next cut (or a `workflow_dispatch` run) is the full check.\n- `actionlint` is not installed on this machine.\n\n## Notes\n\n- The issue says that the Zola part of the test is \"skippable when the binary is absent, as today\". It is not: without Zola, the five Zola tests error (`FileNotFoundError`), they do not skip. This PR does not change that, because the job always has Zola. The README now says so.\n- A `.github/` change from a fork: read, not built. It waits for the maintainer (`needs-maintainer`).\n- `xtask/` is a process file (the new test). The PR does not edit `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION`. A fork needs no action.\n- Branch base: `upstream/main`. No context scout ran; this session did its own searches.\n\nProcess change: yes\nChangelog: none\nEffort: low\n\nFixes #1832\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
